(7354399, 1150217, 138630, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Jules1x:</b></div><hr/><i>. . .  The main part of this image that really didn''t connect with me was the blur of the whites of the shirts, it was just too big a white blur and then at the next second below were bike tires almost in focus.  Was just a bit to uneven for me I think. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yep, the white shirts looked almost blown and were really distracting.  Haven''t read other comments, but what if you put a green layer over the whole and blended it in?  Or crop just below the shirts?  Or both?</td>', 'Originally posted by Jules1x:. . .  The main part of this image that really didn''t connect with me was the blur of the whites of the shirts, it was just too big a white blur and then at the next second below were bike tires almost in focus.  Was just a bit to uneven for me I think.   Yep, the white shirts looked almost blown and were really distracting.  Haven''t read other comments, but what if you put a green layer over the whole and blended it in?  Or crop just below the shirts?  Or both?', '2015-05-27 23:24:53.000000', NULL, 0),
