(7377739, 1150189, 115814, '<td valign="top">OK,<br/> <br/><b>From the DPL Critique Club</b>: This is a strong entry for the Abstract in Green challenge. I had no idea you could get this type of effect with just water and cream. Very nice. What I like is the randomness of the submerged form. It tells an interesting story about the fluid dynamics. While the background yellow blends well with the green, I wonder what a more contrasting color might have done here. Finally, the shapes in the background are effective, but they appear to not be symmetrical from left to right. This may be a result of the mass of cream being larger on the right and obscuring the background. I do like the color gradient change in the background, your gel use was effective in creating this lighting pattern.</td>', 'OK, From the DPL Critique Club: This is a strong entry for the Abstract in Green challenge. I had no idea you could get this type of effect with just water and cream. Very nice. What I like is the randomness of the submerged form. It tells an interesting story about the fluid dynamics. While the background yellow blends well with the green, I wonder what a more contrasting color might have done here. Finally, the shapes in the background are effective, but they appear to not be symmetrical from left to right. This may be a result of the mass of cream being larger on the right and obscuring the background. I do like the color gradient change in the background, your gel use was effective in creating this lighting pattern.', '2015-06-30 15:10:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(7378043, 1150198, 115814, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the DPC Critique Club</b>:<br/> <br/>I realize that this is late in coming, but Critique Club members have been backlogged with current challenges and recently got caught up enough to go back a bit in the request queue. I voted in this challenge and gave you a 9. Absolutely loved this shot. It''s at an unusual angle and didn''t immediately give itself up as a bottle and cap. Once that became clear the technical excellence became even more apparent. Amazing sharpness and detail, perfect strobe technique and spot on exposure. I don''t think I can tell you a thing that would make it better, or would explain your lower end votes. Maybe chalk it up to a commonplace subject that was easily identified, and therefore not abstract enough. Who knows. It''s a great photo. I''d be proud as heck if I was behind the lens. Kudos.</td>', 'Greetings from the DPC Critique Club: I realize that this is late in coming, but Critique Club members have been backlogged with current challenges and recently got caught up enough to go back a bit in the request queue. I voted in this challenge and gave you a 9. Absolutely loved this shot. It''s at an unusual angle and didn''t immediately give itself up as a bottle and cap. Once that became clear the technical excellence became even more apparent. Amazing sharpness and detail, perfect strobe technique and spot on exposure. I don''t think I can tell you a thing that would make it better, or would explain your lower end votes. Maybe chalk it up to a commonplace subject that was easily identified, and therefore not abstract enough. Who knows. It''s a great photo. I''d be proud as heck if I was behind the lens. Kudos.', '2015-06-30 20:37:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(7379271, 1149983, 46918, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club...<br/> <br/>You are right this is more of a macro than an abstract. However it still works as an abstract for me. The quality of the picture is great. Nice crisp lines and colors. I even like the water droplets. I may have brought the crop in a little bit on the left though. Happy shooting.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club... You are right this is more of a macro than an abstract. However it still works as an abstract for me. The quality of the picture is great. Nice crisp lines and colors. I even like the water droplets. I may have brought the crop in a little bit on the left though. Happy shooting.', '2015-07-01 15:29:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(7379947, 1150313, 46918, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club...<br/> <br/>Now this is a true abstract. It meets the challenge perfectly. To be quite honest I don''t know why it scored so low. The only thing that I can see that could have been done differently would be a little more of the green in the upper left hand corner. For me that area is a little light. Good job... Happy shooting</td>', 'Hello from the critique club... Now this is a true abstract. It meets the challenge perfectly. To be quite honest I don''t know why it scored so low. The only thing that I can see that could have been done differently would be a little more of the green in the upper left hand corner. For me that area is a little light. Good job... Happy shooting', '2015-07-02 10:22:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7380092, 1150289, 46918, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club...<br/> <br/>You did quite nicely on this shot. To be quite honest it is very difficult for me to give an honest critique of an abstract image. I''ve never been into abstracts too much. However this does look like a wall hanger. It''s got nice flowing color. It also has some depth to it that I like. I hope this critique helped you out.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club... You did quite nicely on this shot. To be quite honest it is very difficult for me to give an honest critique of an abstract image. I''ve never been into abstracts too much. However this does look like a wall hanger. It''s got nice flowing color. It also has some depth to it that I like. I hope this critique helped you out.', '2015-07-02 12:36:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7408457, 1150319, 100831, '<td valign="top">What rhythm!  I hear music in this.</td>', 'What rhythm!  I hear music in this.', '2015-10-06 23:24:12.000000', NULL, 0);
